--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE SHAPE (what parity means here)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TeslaRegionPage.tsx (31 lines) is a first-class page wrapper:
  • usePageTitle(t('region.title','Region & API'))
  • <PageContainer title={t('region.title')} subtitle={t('region.subtitle', 'Tesla account
        region and Fleet API endpoint')}>
       <RegionSettings />
    </PageContainer>
It carries NO API hook of its own (RegionSettings owns useTeslaUserRegion/useRefreshTeslaRegion).
So the page parity unit = the page chrome (the two strings region.title / region.subtitle, in the
same grouping/order) + the embedded RegionSettings panel. The manifest record confirms this:
"strings": ["region.subtitle","region.title"], requiredCount 2, no panels/charts/maps/data sources.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`. That path is
NOT a project.yml source group in this repo. The real, COMPILED canonical admin-page home is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — where the live sibling P7 admin pages ship (ApiPlayground,
DiskForecast, FleetTelemetryCoverage, LiveSignalInspector, SchemaDrift; apps/parity/apple-ledger.json
shows all five "done"), and which project.yml lists as a `Sources` source path. The page therefore
ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Admin`. Strings ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings`
(an allowed file). This is the SAME reconciliation the DiskForecast / SchemaDrift sibling logs recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the top-level path `/tesla-region` (the Region & API page, promoted
out of the Settings "Integrations" group). Exactly as the SchemaDrift / LiveSignalInspector siblings
did for their routes, TeslaRegion gets a dedicated `.teslaRegion` AppRoute case (pathSegment
"tesla-region"). `AppRouteParser` resolves `/tesla-region -> .teslaRegion` via its canonical path
segment (no alias needed — the segment matches 1:1). `TeslaRegionRouteRegistration` hosts the page on
that route; it is composed into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift, so the page is reachable via the
System-group sidebar entry, the iPhone "More" list, the command palette, and any `/tesla-region` deep
link. The new case is placed in the `.system` group with siblings admin/apiPlayground/schemaDrift/etc.

NATIVE RegionSettings COMPONENT REUSE: the embedded panel is the already-shipped native RegionSettings
(P3 component unit) in TeslaSync/feature-views/RegionSettings{,.Model,.Adapter,.Views}.swift. The page
constructs it through a composition-time `SampleRegionSettingsSource` default (a representative SI-free
region snapshot — na / fleet-api.prd.na.vn.cloud.tesla.com) so the embedded panel renders its populated
data state out of the box (ADR-011 — never a blank surface), mirroring the sibling admin pages'
`Sample…DataSource` defaults. Production injects the KMP-backed useTeslaUserRegion adapter at the
registration seam (TeslaRegionRouteRegistration.registry(source:)).

